{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T16:19:52.261Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"eda2446424a05ba568a1cb08","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.314","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-4zpq71"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"pm config set on a schema-invalid settings.json writes the fallback defaults as the whole file, deleting unrelated settings"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"When `settings.json` is valid JSON but fails schema validation (for example an unknown value in a validated enum such as `context.next_ranking_policy`, `validation.parent_reference` or `item_format`), `readSettingsWithMetadata` returns `buildFallbackSettingsReadResult(\"settings_read_invalid_schema\")`. That result is the full default settings with no persistence snapshot. A following `pm config project set <key> <value>` then writes those defaults as the complete document, silently removing every unrelated stored setting. The existing write guard refuses only malformed JSON (`settings_read_invalid_json`), not schema-invalid JSON.\n\npm-x2aplf fixed the same overwrite for valid sparse files (persist only the changed key). Its acceptance criteria do not cover the invalid-schema read path. CodeRabbit found this on PR #1638: the new `context.next_ranking_policy` enum adds one more way to reach it, but the behaviour predates that change and applies to every validated setting."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["config","data-integrity","review","settings"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-31T16:19:52.261Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T16:19:52.261Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A config write against a settings.json that fails schema validation is refused with a code naming the invalid field (no write), or preserves the original document and changes only the requested key; a regression test seeds a schema-invalid settings.json with unrelated keys, runs pm config project set, and asserts the unrelated keys survive or the write is refused; the same holds for SDK config writers"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-o2kc"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"No configuration write ever replaces a stored settings.json with fallback defaults; schema-invalid settings are refused with a field-naming error or preserved byte-for-byte outside the written key."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-x2aplf","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-31T16:19:52.261Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"4e1b31dcdf209079a73a4baaaff1deb7db8ee24dc7d97bc8154a4f8045e3c24a","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"5d2397d076afc91044df3bc8a3024d5cb487ae281916ac3bccb1e1ddb54fb1eb"}
