{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T14:03:49.001Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"489489c9e2938b0738fed20a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-01T14:03:49.000Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"PR 1648 review follow-up (owner verification comment): an explicit repair to the DEFAULT value could not repair an invalid stored field, because the defaults-to-proposed delta is empty when the assigned value equals the default; pm config set even reported changed: false with no write. Fix: writeSettings(pmRoot, settings, op, { assignedPaths }) applies explicitly assigned dotted paths over an unreadable document even when equal to the default (readable documents ignore the option; unsafe segments refuse with settings_write_assigned_path_invalid). pm config <scope> set <dotted.key> passes its path and reports changed: true; every other pm config setter now writes over a fallback so it returns the typed settings_write_invalid_existing_schema refusal instead of a silent changed: false. Snapshot-only SDK repairs to the default still refuse truthfully with the field named. Covered in tests/unit/core/store/settings-fallback-write.spec.ts (default-valued and non-default repairs, cached reads, unchanged history on refusal, CLI default repair and two setter no-op refusals)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T14:03:49.001Z"}],"before_hash":"f81488bfd622cdb4e737bfbf31b2ee3c719407ebcd29f95031018f5a0f9a8ea7","after_hash":"3570b77ce8796c1d26b44b812f13ded4281c1fc3f3ac7238fc7112fce961ca5e","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d33f60a4ba50f083dc24d8339c0ade003d7b360b068116dfd36090c0f718658c"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T14:03:49.599Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"489489c9e2938b0738fed20a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A config write against a settings.json that fails schema validation is refused with a code naming the invalid field (no write), or preserves the original document and changes only the requested key; a regression test seeds a schema-invalid settings.json with unrelated keys, runs pm config project set, and asserts the unrelated keys survive or the write is refused; the same holds for SDK config writers; An explicit repair to the default value takes effect: pm config <scope> set <dotted.key> <default> repairs the stored field with changed: true and keeps unrelated keys, SDK callers pass writeSettings options.assignedPaths, and no pm config setter reports a silent changed: false over an unreadable document"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T14:03:49.599Z"}],"before_hash":"3570b77ce8796c1d26b44b812f13ded4281c1fc3f3ac7238fc7112fce961ca5e","after_hash":"352f5ccd07019de3e1664024732da181423a03f8cf97c8e7e850e87b7d8afdff","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"43e592d46dc028e6a45d50c2d79549d56b70fa93f4f16a97f7eb734897fbdbe2"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T15:40:55.396Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"489489c9e2938b0738fed20a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-01T15:40:55.396Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"PR 1648 review follow-up (CodeRabbit). Every specialized pm config setter now passes the settings paths it assigns (for example sprint_release_format_policy assigns validation.sprint_release_format, governance policy setters assign governance.preset plus their field, the context setter assigns each provided option, item_format assigns item_format), so setting a default value repairs that field through any setter, not only pm config set <dotted.key>. A setter that keeps the default of a different invalid field still returns the typed refusal. After a successful write from a fallback object, its next write measures the change from the document it last wrote instead of from the defaults, so a peer's later edit to a field this object already wrote is kept. The refusal's next steps no longer promise an assigned-path repair for every field: a record key containing a dot cannot be addressed that way, so the first step is to fix or remove the field in settings.json, with pm config named only for configurable settings. Ordering note: gate_evidence and escape_class were recorded after close and release because the defect-evidence gate first failed on the hosted run; they are follow-up records, the append-only history is unchanged."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T15:40:55.396Z"}],"before_hash":"352f5ccd07019de3e1664024732da181423a03f8cf97c8e7e850e87b7d8afdff","after_hash":"5a74214ebeea9df1125e9504be61c7e6ff7f71408aea779db84427789402faf4","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ee815c3704ed1dc04ef851f31b796bfa02001c0d899ee83d9c9fbf579c01ee57"}
